# MUSAEUS — what semgrep may not look at.
#
# The point of this file is a single line near the bottom: `!tests/`.
#
# semgrep ships default excludes that contain `tests/`. Creating any
# .semgrepignore replaces those defaults wholesale, so this file must also
# restate the ordinary noise directories -- otherwise "fixing" the tests gap
# would start linting .venv and node_modules.
#
# M-11, 2026-09-08: the README documented
#     semgrep --config .semgrep/rules.yml musaeus/ scripts/ tests/
# and called the result clean. It was clean because the third path scanned
# ZERO files -- 136 scanned, none from tests/ -- and `--no-git-ignore` does
# not lift a semgrepignore. An ERROR-severity rule had never examined the
# tree it actually matches in, and the passing exit code said so every time.

.git/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
build/
dist/

# Re-included deliberately. These rules guard against re-implementing a
# thing the repo already owns -- reading a duration, adding a DB column --
# and a test that hand-rolls one can drift from the real definition exactly
# as production code can. Where a test genuinely needs to, it says so with
# an inline `# nosemgrep:` and a reason, which is a recorded decision rather
# than a silent gap.
!tests/

# Vendored ORPHEUS code, excluded on purpose and worth stating rather than
# leaving to a default. These rules say "do not re-implement what the repo
# already owns", and vendoring IS a deliberate re-implementation: the files
# run standalone and cannot import musaeus. Their duplication is pinned by
# tests instead -- see tests/test_car_duration_tolerance_is_one_rule.py,
# which asserts the vendored tolerance rule matches musaeus/duration.py
# across ten values. That test is the guard here, not this linter.
#
# Until 2026-09-08 this directory was excluded by accident, along with
# tests/, by semgrep's bundled defaults. Fixing the tests gap exposed three
# findings in here that had never been reported. The exclusion stays; the
# reason is now written down.
scripts/car_library/vendor/
